hen the agent's state first holds its db (a spawn, a resume, a clone), and ``seon.ctx/patch`` keeps it from each transaction's datoms, which ``seon.agent/transact!`` records with the db they made. The walk's state (`:ix`) knows where each entity is held, its pattern, and which `[attribute value]` each join watches (a reverse join's ref to it, a lookup's name). A datom touches a held entity (its own attributes, a forward join) or a watched join; the patch rebuilds each touched entity where it is held, shortest path first, as a build would, keeping every join and member nothing touched, and copies the path above it. A rebuilt entity keeps every attribute equal to before as the object it was, and a rebuild that changes nothing is the old node. A move with no transaction (a merge of main, a resume) is patched from the datoms the two values differ by. A change of the pattern, or one that moves where an entity is held (a new run reaching the task, the holder leaving its window), builds the record anew, as a fresh build places it, and shares back every subtree it did not change (the same objects): that patch costs the record, once a run." "docs/render.md#reactive-renders 16%: A render reads ctx as Reagent's components read a ratom: ```seon.ratom``` is reagent.ratom ported (`RAtom`, `Reaction`, `run-in-reaction`, `flush!`, `dispose!`; Reagent's own tests, `seon.ratom-test`), with the cursor inferred (owner, 2026-10-26: \"I'd rather infer the cursor than require it\")." "docs/render.md#components 14%: A component is a call in hiccup, `[f opts & children]` (Reagent's form), of a render whose opts declare what it reads: `:seon.ctx/ctx`, ctx as a tracking view ([reactive renders](#reactive-renders)), or `:seon.db/db`, the branch's db, read under `d/with-reads`." "docs/render.md#the-models-context-a-cached-prefix-then-the-turn 12%: A model request sends what does not change first, so the provider serves it from its prefix cache, and sends nothing twice."], :functions [["seon.ren