/merged-t :seon.run/outcome :seon.run/reason :seon.run/status :seon.task/kind]] "my.agent/asked 4%: The name sym is asked by: the var it resolves to in the agent's namespace (an alias, 'str/join, read as clojure.string/join, the name its callers' facts record), else sym as written." ["seon.prove/result-tx 4%: The facts a finished run leaves on main: one :seon.proof/ result per test that ran or was reused (a green the results directory held becomes a fact too) at its digest, greens and reds, and the run's fact." [:seon.proof.run/branch :seon.proof.run/error :seon.proof.run/fail :seon.proof.run/id :seon.proof.run/ms :seon.proof.run/pass :seon.proof.run/skipped-process :seon.proof.run/t :seon.proof/branch :seon.proof/change :seon.proof/digest :seon.proof/failures :seon.proof/latest :seon.proof/run :seon.proof/status :seon.proof/t :seon.proof/test]]], :schemas [[:my.agent/no-var "50%"] [:seon.proof/status "10%"] [:seon.config.ai/provider "6%"] [:seon.config.ctx/callers "6%"] [:seon.config.source/process-vars "5%"]]}}
{:task "seon.proofs/a-failed-import-leaves-no-branch", :plan "Done (2026-10-25, root's two fixes): test-runner/program-db makes the tree's facts from the parent branch before it makes the tree's branch (a file that does not read throws first), and a refused transaction deletes the branch it made (a finally on a success flag, no catch); a test namespace the program db holds no test of fails the plan, named (test-runner/tests-of's :no-test), exit 1, never an empty OK. A store made before the fix may still hold a partial branch: the plan now fails on it by name. Found by form-keywords, 2026-10-25: test-runner/program-db makes the tree's branch (d/branch!) before it transacts that tree's import, so when the transact fails (here Datahike refused a :form/keywords value: datahike.transaction/a-keyword-attributes-two-values-are-two-values), the branch stays, named for the tree, empty or behind. The next plan of a changed tree branches from it as the kept tree of the fewest changed files and refreshes only those, so its program db holds only the namespaces changed since: `bin/test seon.program-test` selected 0 tests and said TEST OK, and datahike.query-test, untouched, selected 0. Fix at the producer: the branch exists only once its import committed (transact on a branch named for the tree only after, or delete the branch when the transact throws, as the one edge function the failure-points page names). Proof: a plan whose import throws leaves the store's branches as they were, and the next plan of the same program finds every test namespace.", :changed #{"docs/source.md#tests-run-by-reach"}, :shown {:sections ["docs/agent.md#what-you-read 25%: Your context comes in two parts: the run's, sent once and unchanged while you work, then the turn's, measured again after each of your replies." "docs/source.md#tests-run-by-reach 25%: A test runs only when something it reaches changed since it was last green, in any checkout (task `seon.program/tests-run-by-reach`). ```seon.program/r